@startuml class-extractors
title The concrete extractors, and how they nest

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "base/extractor" <<Frame>> {

  class "StructExtraction<'ast>" as Struct {
    +derive_input: &'ast DeriveInput
    +fields: Vec<Extracted<FieldExtraction, &'ast Field>>
    --
    Extractor<&'ast DeriveInput>
    Output = Extracted<Self, &'ast DeriveInput>
    Sourced::Source = DeriveInput
    Validate::Valid = &'ast DataStruct
  }

  class "FieldExtraction<'ast>" as Field {
    +field: &'ast Field
    +transformation: Vec<Extracted<TransformationExtraction, &'ast Attribute>>
    --
    Extractor<&'ast Field>
    Output = Extracted<Self, &'ast Field>
    Sourced::Source = Field
    Validate::Valid = &'ast Field
  }

  class "TransformationExtraction<'ast>" as Transform #FFD9D9 {
    +attribute: &'ast Attribute
    +expression: &'ast Expr
    --
    extract_from = **todo!()**
  }
}

package "base/syntax" <<Frame>> {

  class "SyntaxFieldAttributeExtraction<'ast, S>" as Syntax #FFF4E5 {
    -attribute: &'ast Attribute
    -kind: SyntaxFieldAttributeKind<'ast, S>
    --
    Extractor<&'ast Attribute> **for S = Raw**
    +kind() -> &SyntaxFieldAttributeKind
    +resolve() -> Extraction<..Parsed>
  }

  enum "SyntaxFieldAttributeKind<'ast, S>" as Kind {
    Shape(S::Item<'ast, syn::Type>)
    Alias(S::Item<'ast, Ident>)
  }
}

Struct *-- "0..*" Field : extract_each
Field *-- "0..*" Transform : extract_each
Syntax *-- Kind

note right of Struct
  ""fields"" is already written in the shape
  ""#[from = source.data.fields]"" will generate:
  ""extract_each::<FieldExtraction, _, _>(..)"".
  The designer names WHERE the children are;
  the ""Vec"" in the type picks the helper; the
  walk is not written out.

  The turbofish is not noise — ""T::Output"" is an
  associated type and so not injective, so the
  extractor cannot be inferred from the field.
  Generated code always knows it.
end note

note as Deleted
  **Deleted as stale scaffolding**
  SyntaxExtraction, SyntaxAttributeExtraction,
  SyntaxFieldExtraction — they held
  ""Vec<Extraction<..>>"" where every extractor
  now yields ""Extracted<.., &'ast Node>"", and
  SyntaxAttributeExtraction held an
  ""alias: &'ast Ident"" that cannot exist (an
  ident parsed out of tokens is not in the AST).
  None had an Extractor impl to keep it honest.
end note

note bottom of Transform
  Signature is correct, body is not written.
  It will PANIC if reached — nothing reaches
  it today. Under the corrected boundary it
  stops being a bespoke Meta matcher and
  becomes "read grammar type G from an
  opening", which is processor work.
  (#attribute/generic-grammar)
end note

note bottom of Syntax
  Extraction always lands in ""Raw"" — forced,
  not chosen: only ""Raw"" can build an item out
  of loose tokens, so a ""Stage""-generic
  ""extract_from"" could not construct its own
  payload. Moving to ""Parsed"" is ""resolve""'s job.

  ""Validate"" here answers "is this attribute
  MINE?", narrowing to
  ""(&Attribute, SyntaxHelper)"" — a real
  narrowing, so no later stage repeats the
  comparison. The head match comes from a
  ""vocabulary!"", so adding a helper breaks the
  build at every site (E0004).

  An unrecognised head is passed over in
  SILENCE: rustc already rejects a head nobody
  registered, so one that reaches us belongs to
  another macro. A doc comment is an attribute,
  and the earlier UnknownKey here fired on every
  documented field. (#heads-are-rustcs)
end note

note as Foreign
  **A doc comment is an attribute.**
  Reporting unowned heads as UnknownKey fired
  on every documented field. That is why
  ""Validate"" filters and ""extract_from"" returns
  an empty extraction rather than a complaint.
end note

Foreign .. Syntax

@enduml
